&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Working at CreateFuture&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://createfuture.com/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;CreateFuture&lt;/a&gt; is an&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;AI-native consulting partner&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;where people do work that matters and are supported to do it well. We work alongside organisations such as PayPal, adidas, NatWest, FanDuel and Money Saving Expert, building digital products and services that make a difference&amp;nbsp; while always putting people first.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re a team of creators. We write code, shape delivery, build go-to-market strategies, develop AI solutions and create the practices that support our people. We work side by side with our clients, challenging what’s not working and helping them to build the future. Our commitment to craft, quality, and culture has helped us scale to over 600 people in just a few years.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;CreateFuture is a &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.greatplacetowork.co.uk/certified-company/1572759&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Great Place to Work-Certified™ company &lt;/a&gt;and has won Best Workplaces UK multiple years in a row.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Join us on our journey. Let’s create tomorrow, together, today.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;_1bsb1osq _18s8y1gf _p12fukw8&quot; data-testid=&quot;view-page-labels-container&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;styles--2BkR3&quot; data-ui=&quot;job-description&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role and team:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Lead Data Engineer to own the technical direction of a data engagement, working with AWS data services, platforms like Snowflake and Databricks, Python, and PySpark across our data team. You’ll lead a team of data engineers, setting the standards for how pipelines and architecture are designed, built, and operated, while staying hands-on with the most complex technical challenges. You’ll work closely with client stakeholders and CreateFuture’s wider engineering capability to make sure delivery is both technically excellent and commercially sound.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll be doing:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the technical direction of a data engagement, setting standards for pipeline architecture, data modelling, orchestration, testing, and operational readiness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and technically direct a team of data engineers, allocating work, reviewing designs and code, and unblocking technical challenges&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and evolve data platform architecture on AWS (e.g. AWS Glue, EMR, S3/Lake Formation, Redshift, Athena) alongside platforms such as Snowflake and Databricks, weighing trade-offs in performance, cost, and maintainability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set and enforce CI/CD, testing, observability, and operational practices across the engagement’s data engineering workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build professional relationships with key client stakeholders, translating business and data requirements into a coherent technical roadmap, with clear estimates, trade-offs, and risks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot and resolve the most complex issues in live data pipelines, and lead incident response when things go wron&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We&#39;d love to talk to you if you:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have extensive hands-on experience designing and operating production data platforms on a modern cloud data stack such as AWS (Glue, EMR, Redshift, S3/Lake Formation), Databricks, Snowflake, or comparable, and can articulate which architectural decisions travel between platforms and which don’t&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have deep SQL expertise and a strong grasp of data modelling and architecture (Kimball, data vault, medallion/lakehouse patterns, or domain modelling). This is the clearest line between someone who operates a platform and someone who can design on top of it, and it’s provider-agnostic&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have owned orchestration strategy in production, including dependency design, retries, SLAs, and the observability that tells you a pipeline failed before the client does&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have designed ingestion from awkward sources (APIs, CDC off operational databases, files that change shape without warning) and set patterns your team can reuse&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have strong proficiency in Python and PySpark for batch/ELT processing at scale, with production-grade, well-tested code. The bulk of this work is batch and ELT, but you’ll have experience with event-driven or micro-batch pipelines and know where the design assumptions stop holding&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have led or technically directed a team of data engineers, setting standards for pipeline design, testing, and delivery, and growing the engineers around you&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have owned CI/CD and operational practices for data engineering workflows across a team or engagement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are experienced working directly with client stakeholders, building trust, shaping solutions from ambiguous requirements, and challenging where appropriate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
